        <mxCell id="c241" value="&lt;i&gt;A finished answer: one row for each of the 12 relationships, with counts of rows, blanks and orphans and a reason for every blank. The PivotTable below the log lists the 71 AccountID values the ledger uses, and each is looked up in the AccountID column of Account (the formula bar shows the lookup of the first). Outlined: the Orphans and Verdict columns, and the lookup, whose 0 misses are counted in the last row.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="729" width="860" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
